   answer="Potassium, magnesium and calcium are taken up through the same doors in the root, so too much of one shuts out the others. Heavy potash brings on magnesium shortage, and an imbalance between magnesium and calcium can show symptoms that are treated with the wrong nutrient. A soil test that shows all three together is the way to see the balance.",
